# mcp__ripwire_for — ripwire/for

Task-lens ranked, signatures-only inventory of the building blocks most relevant to a task (cx=complexity, in=reuse-count). task = the task in plain words; budget_tokens = an optional ceiling (the CLI --for --token-budget). The header carries route= (which ranker answered, and why), confidence=/margin_pct= (how sharp the ranked head is — low means a starting point, not an answer) and lens= (the per-row columns this dialect does not measure).

## Schema
```ts
type Args = {
  /** a STRING repo directory */
  path?: string;
  /** an ARRAY of 1..16 repo roots */
  paths?: string[];
  /** the task in plain words */
  task: string;
  /** a positive integer token budget (omit it for the verb's own default) */
  budget_tokens?: number;
  /** a BOOLEAN: true forces plain subtoken+body BM25 (omit it for the default router) */
  no_route?: boolean;
  /** a positive integer (omit for the default window) */
  limit?: number;
  /** a non-negative integer (omit to start at row 1) */
  offset?: number;
  /** lego, compose, or both */
  sections?: string;
};
```
Execute by writing JSON to xd://mcp__ripwire_for.

