# mcp__ripwire_grep — ripwire/grep

Trigram literal search; each hit annotated with its enclosing symbol (which function/class it is in). pattern = the literal; in=any lifts the span tiering (by default the tightest non-empty tier is served and what was held back rides as suppressed_comment/suppressed_string); limit/offset page the hits (first 100, has_more/next_offset end the loop). total/shown/capped/hits_capped and complete= are defined in the answer's own legend.

## Schema
```ts
type Args = {
  /** a STRING repo directory */
  path?: string;
  /** an ARRAY of 1..16 repo roots */
  paths?: string[];
  /** a literal string to search for */
  pattern: string;
  /** which span tier to serve: code (default) or any */
  in?: string;
  /** a positive integer (omit for the default window) */
  limit?: number;
  /** a non-negative integer (omit to start at row 1) */
  offset?: number;
};
```
Execute by writing JSON to xd://mcp__ripwire_grep.

