1:# Cross-Platform Matrix — organizer-add-athlete-consent-20261005
2:
3:| Platform | Organizer Add Athlete | Player consent/claim | Compatibility |
4:|---|---|---|---|
5:| Web organizer | Full 3-mode modal in RegistrationTab beside unchanged Excel import; uses ParticipantIdentity | registration checkbox becomes optional; self-consent/claim pages call same API | new participant fields optional; existing names preserved |
6:| Web player | no organizer action | current user sees one-way consent; guest claim URL lands on verified account path | missing optional fields tolerated |
7:| Flutter organizer | No new screen unless current code inventory shows an equivalent surface; current organizer ops is not the registration tab | n/a | no incompatible model required |
8:| Flutter player | retain registration flows; explicit opt-in checkbox optional and never blocks registration; add API/model support to refresh own consent | consent status actionable on player-owned registration surface; email claim URL may open Web | `rankingConsent` request field remains optional; additive fields nullable |
9:
10:## Responsive and accessibility
11:
12:Web: verify desktop and narrow viewport, keyboard/tab/focus, screen reader names, touch controls. Flutter: verify tap target, semantics, loading/error, reduced motion and offline retry. No visual compliance claim without runtime screenshots.
13:
14:## Locale/date
15:
16:Keep existing localized keys/add matching Web and Flutter strings. Server timestamps are ISO-8601 UTC; display in user's locale only at presentation.

